{"title":"Formula Sheet","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Formula Sheet","author":"Sugeng Riyanto, M.Sc.","date":"2026","format":{"pdf":{"toc":false},"html":{"toc":true}}},"headingText":"Mechanics","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\n### Motion\n- Average speed: $v = \\frac{s}{t}$\n- Acceleration: $a = \\frac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta t}$\n- $v^2 = u^2 + 2as$\n- $s = ut + \\frac{1}{2}at^2$\n\n### Forces\n- Weight: $W = mg$\n- Force: $F = ma$\n- Momentum: $p = mv$\n- Impulse: $F\\Delta t = \\Delta p$\n- Resultant force: $F = \\frac{\\Delta p}{\\Delta t}$\n\n### Energy and Power\n- Kinetic energy: $E_k = \\frac{1}{2}mv^2$\n- Gravitational potential energy: $\\Delta E_p = mg\\Delta h$\n- Work done: $W = Fd$\n- Power: $P = \\frac{W}{t} = \\frac{\\Delta E}{t}$\n- Efficiency: $\\text{Efficiency} = \\frac{\\text{useful energy output}}{\\text{total energy input}} \\times 100\\%$\n\n### Pressure\n- Pressure: $p = \\frac{F}{A}$\n- Pressure in liquids: $\\Delta p = \\rho g \\Delta h$\n\n### Circular Motion\n- Centripetal force: $F = \\frac{mv^2}{r}$\n\n---\n\n## Thermal Physics\n\n### Temperature\n- $T(\\text{K}) = \\theta(°\\text{C}) + 273$\n\n### Thermal Properties\n- Specific heat capacity: $c = \\frac{\\Delta E}{m\\Delta\\theta}$\n- Thermal energy: $\\Delta E = mc\\Delta\\theta$\n\n### Gas Laws\n- $pV = \\text{constant}$ (at constant temperature)\n\n---\n\n## Waves\n\n### Wave Properties\n- Wave speed: $v = f\\lambda$\n- Frequency: $f = \\frac{1}{T}$\n- Refractive index: $n = \\frac{\\sin i}{\\sin r}$\n- Critical angle: $n = \\frac{1}{\\sin c}$\n\n---\n\n## Electricity and Magnetism\n\n### Electrical Quantities\n- Charge: $Q = It$\n- Potential difference: $V = \\frac{W}{Q}$\n- E.m.f.: $E = \\frac{W}{Q}$\n- Resistance: $R = \\frac{V}{I}$\n- Electrical power: $P = IV = I^2R = \\frac{V^2}{R}$\n- Electrical energy: $E = IVt$\n\n### Transformers\n- $\\frac{V_p}{V_s} = \\frac{N_p}{N_s}$\n- For 100% efficiency: $I_pV_p = I_sV_s$\n\n### Magnetic Effects\n- Force on current-carrying conductor: $F = BIl$ (Extended)\n\n---\n\n## Nuclear Physics\n\n### Radioactivity\n- Half-life calculations: $N = N_0 \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n$\n- where $n$ = number of half-lives\n\n---\n\n## Space Physics\n\n### Orbital Motion\n- Average orbital speed: $v = \\frac{2\\pi r}{T}$\n- Hubble's Law: $H_0 = \\frac{v}{d}$\n- Age of Universe: $t \\approx \\frac{1}{H_0}$\n\n---\n\n## Constants\n\n- Speed of light in vacuum: $c = 3.0 \\times 10^8 \\text{ m/s}$\n- Acceleration of free fall: $g = 9.8 \\text{ m/s}^2 \\approx 10 \\text{ m/s}^2$\n- Hubble constant: $H_0 = 2.2 \\times 10^{-18} \\text{ s}^{-1}$\n- 1 light-year: $1 \\text{ ly} = 9.5 \\times 10^{15} \\text{ m}$","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n## Mechanics\n\n### Motion\n- Average speed: $v = \\frac{s}{t}$\n- Acceleration: $a = \\frac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta t}$\n- $v^2 = u^2 + 2as$\n- $s = ut + \\frac{1}{2}at^2$\n\n### Forces\n- Weight: $W = mg$\n- Force: $F = ma$\n- Momentum: $p = mv$\n- Impulse: $F\\Delta t = \\Delta p$\n- Resultant force: $F = \\frac{\\Delta p}{\\Delta t}$\n\n### Energy and Power\n- Kinetic energy: $E_k = \\frac{1}{2}mv^2$\n- Gravitational potential energy: $\\Delta E_p = mg\\Delta h$\n- Work done: $W = Fd$\n- Power: $P = \\frac{W}{t} = \\frac{\\Delta E}{t}$\n- Efficiency: $\\text{Efficiency} = \\frac{\\text{useful energy output}}{\\text{total energy input}} \\times 100\\%$\n\n### Pressure\n- Pressure: $p = \\frac{F}{A}$\n- Pressure in liquids: $\\Delta p = \\rho g \\Delta h$\n\n### Circular Motion\n- Centripetal force: $F = \\frac{mv^2}{r}$\n\n---\n\n## Thermal Physics\n\n### Temperature\n- $T(\\text{K}) = \\theta(°\\text{C}) + 273$\n\n### Thermal Properties\n- Specific heat capacity: $c = \\frac{\\Delta E}{m\\Delta\\theta}$\n- Thermal energy: $\\Delta E = mc\\Delta\\theta$\n\n### Gas Laws\n- $pV = \\text{constant}$ (at constant temperature)\n\n---\n\n## Waves\n\n### Wave Properties\n- Wave speed: $v = f\\lambda$\n- Frequency: $f = \\frac{1}{T}$\n- Refractive index: $n = \\frac{\\sin i}{\\sin r}$\n- Critical angle: $n = \\frac{1}{\\sin c}$\n\n---\n\n## Electricity and Magnetism\n\n### Electrical Quantities\n- Charge: $Q = It$\n- Potential difference: $V = \\frac{W}{Q}$\n- E.m.f.: $E = \\frac{W}{Q}$\n- Resistance: $R = \\frac{V}{I}$\n- Electrical power: $P = IV = I^2R = \\frac{V^2}{R}$\n- Electrical energy: $E = IVt$\n\n### Transformers\n- $\\frac{V_p}{V_s} = \\frac{N_p}{N_s}$\n- For 100% efficiency: $I_pV_p = I_sV_s$\n\n### Magnetic Effects\n- Force on current-carrying conductor: $F = BIl$ (Extended)\n\n---\n\n## Nuclear Physics\n\n### Radioactivity\n- Half-life calculations: $N = N_0 \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n$\n- where $n$ = number of half-lives\n\n---\n\n## Space Physics\n\n### Orbital Motion\n- Average orbital speed: $v = \\frac{2\\pi r}{T}$\n- Hubble's Law: $H_0 = \\frac{v}{d}$\n- Age of Universe: $t \\approx \\frac{1}{H_0}$\n\n---\n\n## Constants\n\n- Speed of light in vacuum: $c = 3.0 \\times 10^8 \\text{ m/s}$\n- Acceleration of free fall: $g = 9.8 \\text{ m/s}^2 \\approx 10 \\text{ m/s}^2$\n- Hubble constant: $H_0 = 2.2 \\times 10^{-18} \\text{ s}^{-1}$\n- 1 light-year: $1 \\text{ ly} = 9.5 \\times 10^{15} \\text{ m}$"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":8,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"png","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":true,"freeze":false,"echo":false,"output":true,"warning":false,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"python":"C:/Users/User/AppData/Local/Programs/Python/Python312/python.exe","message":false,"dpi":300,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":false,"code-overflow":"scrol